  "question": {
    "text": "Two sources of sound&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> are moving towards and away from a stationary observer with the same speed respectively. If the frequency of the sound produced by both the sources is equal to&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>400</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi></math>, then the speed of sources (approximately) if the observer detects 4 beats per second, is [Given, speed of sound <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>340</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>]"
